     "rotation",
     "revolution",
     "axis"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "The Earth rotates, or spins, on its axis once in about 24 hours. This causes day and night: the side facing the Sun has day.\nThe Earth also revolves, or travels, around the Sun once in about 365 and a quarter days, which is one year.\nBecause the axis is tilted as the Earth revolves, we get seasons and the length of day changes."
    }
